sentences.t:
“Nunc, o lecta manus, validis incumbite remis;
tollite, ferte rates; inimicam findite rostris
hanc terram, sulcumque sibi premat ipsa carina.

sentences.l:
“Now, O chosen band, on the strong bend to the oars;
lift, carry the ships; the hostile split with your beaks,
this land, and a furrow for herself let press the keel itself.

sentences.t:
ni fratrum stipata cohors foret obvia, Phorci
progenies, septem numero, septenaque tela
coniciunt;

sentences.l:
had not of brothers a packed band met him, of Phorcus
the offspring, seven in number, and seven spears
they hurl;

sentences.t:
Magno discordes aethere venti
proelia ceu tollunt animis et viribus aequis;
non ipsi inter se, non nubila, non mare cedit;
anceps pugna diu, stant obnixa omnia contra:

sentences.l:
In the great, at strife, sky winds
battles as when raise with spirits and strength equal;
not they themselves to each other, not the clouds, not the sea gives way;
doubtful the fight long, stand straining all things against each other:
